---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const nav = `<strong>Start</strong><a href="/docs">Overview</a><a href="/docs/quickstart">Quickstart</a><strong>Build</strong><a href="/docs/api">API reference</a><a href="/docs/integrations">SDK &amp; frameworks</a><a href="/docs/multilingual">Multilingual</a><strong>Run</strong><a href="/docs/hosting" class="active">Hosting</a><a href="/docs/security">Security</a>`;
---
<Base title="Memflex hosting — laptop to production" desc="$6 VPS to K8s. One SQLite file, almost nothing to operate." path="/docs/hosting">
<div class="wrap" style="padding:64px 24px">
  <span class="eyebrow">Docs · Hosting</span>
  <h1>Laptop to production.</h1>
  <div class="docs-grid" style="margin-top:30px">
    <nav class="docs-nav" set:html={nav}></nav>
    <div class="doc">
      <h2>Docker Compose (recommended start)</h2>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>cp .env.example .env   # fill only keys you use
docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d --build
# API :8000 · console :3001 (compose profile console) · data in reflex-data volume</pre></div>
      <h2>Public URL ($6 VPS + Caddy)</h2>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre># DNS: api.memflex.dev → VPS IP, console.memflex.dev → VPS IP
# Caddyfile (auto-HTTPS):
api.memflex.dev &#123; reverse_proxy localhost:8000 &#125;
console.memflex.dev &#123; reverse_proxy localhost:3001 &#125;</pre></div>
      <h2>Fly / Render / Railway</h2>
      <p>Deploy from repo; persistent disk at <code>/data</code>, <code>REFLEX_DB_PATH=/data/reflex.db</code>. Need scale? Add the compose <code>db</code> service (<code>--profile pg</code>) and set <code>REFLEX_STORE=postgres</code> + <code>REFLEX_POSTGRES_DSN</code> — same API, pgvector speed.</p>
      <h2>Ops signals</h2>
      <p>Backup = copy <code>reflex.db</code> nightly. Scale when <code>/metrics</code> p95 rises. Erasure: <code>DELETE /reflexes/&#123;id&#125;</code>. Full guide: repo <code>docs/HOSTING.md</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</Base>
